---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CtaBand from "../../components/CtaBand.astro";
import PageIntro from "../../components/PageIntro.astro";

/** Partner pages that exist on mersive.com today. */
const ECO = "https://www.mersive.com/ecosystem";
---

<BaseLayout route="resources/ecosystem">
  <PageIntro
    route={"resources/ecosystem"}
    tpl={"T8"}
    title={"The Mersive ecosystem."}
  />
  <p class="dek">
    A Mersive room is rarely only Mersive. It sits between the display, the camera and microphones,
    the mount behind the panel, the signage system that owns the idle screen, and the calendar that
    owns the room. These are the technology partners in each of those five places, and what each
    integration actually does once it is installed.
  </p>
  <p class="note">
    [partner set to be reconciled against mersive.com/ecosystem before publish - product marketing]
  </p>

  <section class="sect reveal flush">
    <div class="kicker">Class one</div>
    <h2>AV peripherals.</h2>
    <p class="sdek">
      The cameras, microphones, speakerphones and soundbars a pod bridges into whatever meeting the
      room is running. Mersive publishes a certified-peripheral list; it is the list this section
      renders, one card per device family.
    </p>
    <div class="cardrow">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="kicker">AV peripherals</div>
        <h3>The certified list</h3>
        <p>
          No partner is named here yet, deliberately. [AV peripheral partner names: pull from the
          certified-peripheral list on mersive.com/ecosystem - product marketing]
        </p>
        <a href={`${ECO}/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">mersive.com/ecosystem ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      A peripheral vendor named on this page is a statement about that company, so this card stays
      empty until the certified list is in hand. Which peripherals a room can use is a support
      question with a documented answer: see <a href="/resources/docs">the documentation hub</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="sect reveal flush">
    <div class="kicker">Class two</div>
    <h2>Digital signage.</h2>
    <p class="sdek">
      Signage partners own the content; Polaris owns the screen. The display a room already has
      publishes the signage system's content while the room is idle, and yields to the meeting the
      moment one starts. Our own signage capability is on
      <a href="/solutions/signage">the digital signage page</a>.
    </p>
    <div class="cardrow">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="kicker">Digital signage</div>
        <h3>Appspace</h3>
        <p>
          Appspace content plays on the Mersive display between meetings, managed in Appspace rather
          than in a second signage tool. [Integration mechanism and setup steps: confirm against the
          partner page - product marketing]
        </p>
        <a href={`${ECO}/appspace/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Appspace partner page ↗</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="kicker">Digital signage</div>
        <h3>Tripleplay</h3>
        <p>
          Tripleplay signage and IPTV content plays on the Mersive display between meetings, driven
          from Tripleplay. [Integration mechanism and setup steps: confirm against the partner page -
          product marketing]
        </p>
        <a href={`${ECO}/tripleplay/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Tripleplay partner page ↗</a>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="kicker">Digital signage</div>
        <h3>22Miles</h3>
        <p>
          Named as a Mersive signage partner. [22Miles: no partner page found on mersive.com;
          integration detail and link owed - product marketing]
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="kicker">Digital signage</div>
        <h3>Carousel</h3>
        <p>
          Named as a Mersive signage partner. [Carousel: no partner page found on mersive.com;
          integration detail and link owed - product marketing]
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="kicker">Digital signage</div>
        <h3>Signagelive</h3>
        <p>
          Named as a Mersive signage partner. [Signagelive: no partner page found on mersive.com;
          integration detail and link owed - product marketing]
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sect reveal flush">
    <div class="kicker">Class three</div>
    <h2>Mounts.</h2>
    <p class="sdek">
      Where the pod physically goes. It matters more than it sounds: an unmounted pod behind a panel
      is the thing that goes missing, and a mount that does not take a lock is a pod that walks.
    </p>
    <div class="cardrow">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="kicker">Mounts</div>
        <h3>Peerless-AV</h3>
        <p>
          The ACC-MSP mounts the pod to a wall or to a Peerless-AV display mount, and is
          Kensington-lock compatible, so the pod is fixed and secured behind the panel rather than
          resting on top of it.
        </p>
        <a href={`${ECO}/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">mersive.com/ecosystem ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sect reveal flush">
    <div class="kicker">Class four</div>
    <h2>Calendaring.</h2>
    <p class="sdek">
      The room's calendar is what turns a display into a room. Sync it and the idle screen stops
      being decoration: it says what this room is doing next, and starts the meeting in one step.
    </p>
    <div class="cardrow">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="kicker">Calendaring</div>
        <h3>Microsoft Exchange / Microsoft 365</h3>
        <p>
          The room resource's calendar syncs to the pod: the display shows the room's status and its
          next meeting, and the meeting on the calendar starts in one step rather than being dialled
          by hand.
        </p>
        <a href="/solutions/signage">Room status on the display →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      [Google Workspace calendaring: mersive.com/ecosystem lists Microsoft only - confirm whether
      Google is supported before this section publishes - product marketing]
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="sect reveal flush">
    <div class="kicker">Class five</div>
    <h2>Conferencing.</h2>
    <p class="sdek">
      The room audio and the call. Polaris bridges the room's own microphones and speakers into
      whatever platform the meeting is running on, chosen per meeting rather than per room: see
      <a href="/products/hybrid">Link &amp; Host</a>.
    </p>
    <div class="cardrow">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="kicker">Conferencing</div>
        <h3>Yamaha</h3>
        <p>
          Yamaha room audio: the room's Yamaha microphones and speakers are carried into the call the
          pod is bridging, so the meeting uses the room's audio rather than a laptop's. [Supported
          Yamaha models and any certification claim - product marketing]
        </p>
        <a href={`${ECO}/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">mersive.com/ecosystem ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="cnv-band green reveal">
    <div class="kicker" style="color:#7ce3a8">Why the list is short</div>
    <h2>Every name on this page is a claim about another company.</h2>
    <p>
      This page lists only partners published on mersive.com. Where a partner page exists, the card
      links to it; where one does not, the card says so instead of describing an integration nobody
      has confirmed. A plausible-looking partner logo is the easiest thing on a website to add and
      the most expensive thing to be wrong about.
    </p>
    <p style="margin:0">
      <a href={`${ECO}/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">The current ecosystem page ↗</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="two">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Selling or installing Polaris?</h3>
      <p>Integrators and resellers work through the partner program, not this page.</p>
      <a href="/partners/program">Partner program →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Building on the platform?</h3>
      <p>The cloud API is enabled per organisation: device power, display info, signage URL, room calendars.</p>
      <a href="/platform/cloud">Polaris Cloud →</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <CtaBand />
</BaseLayout>
